  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return, as their income falls within the tax-exempt threshold.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals with a taxable income not exceeding ₱250,000 are exempt from income tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to Section 24 of the NIRC, the income tax rates for individuals specify that for the taxable year 2023 and onwards, individuals earning not over ₱250,000 are subject to a 0% tax rate. Therefore, if an individual's gross compensation income is exactly ₱250,000, they do not have any taxable income and are not required to file an income tax return.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that individuals earning up to ₱250,000 from compensation are relieved from the obligation of filing an income tax return, provided that their income is solely from one employer and the correct amount of tax has been withheld. This simplifies compliance for low-income earners, allowing them to avoid the administrative burden of filing a return.",
